@startuml
!include style.puml
title Task lifecycle and who may move a task

hide empty description
[*] --> ToDo : PM creates task\n(>=1 acceptance criterion,\nassignee is a developer)
state "To Do" as ToDo
state "In Progress" as InProgress
state "In Review" as InReview
state "Done" as Done

ToDo --> InProgress : assigned developer\nstart (state_change)
InProgress --> InReview : assigned developer\nsubmit (submission event,\nreferences matching check result)
InReview --> Done : product manager\napprove (state_change)
InReview --> InProgress : product manager\nrequest changes\n(review_feedback, 1-5,000 chars)
Done --> [*]

note right of InProgress
  Only while In Progress may the developer
  attach / replace commits.
  Progress updates and AI checks never
  change state.
end note
note bottom of Done
  Every write sends {state, version}.
  A stale version returns 409 VERSION_CONFLICT;
  a disallowed move returns 403 FORBIDDEN.
end note
@enduml
